AetherSDR - experimental digital FM test build (Windows x64)
Source revision: @REVISION@

Getting started
1. Extract the ENTIRE ZIP to a writable folder. Do not run inside the ZIP.
2. Run Start-AetherSDR-HD.cmd. It keeps test settings in this folder's profile
   subfolder and starts disconnected. Running AetherSDR.exe directly instead
   uses your normal Windows AetherSDR settings.
3. Release the RTL-SDR from other SDR software before connecting it here.
   The USB device needs a working compatible WinUSB driver already installed.
   This package does not install or change drivers. Follow your dongle vendor's
   instructions if Windows does not show it as an available RTL receiver.
4. Connect the RTL-SDR, select WFM, and tune a local FM station carrying digital broadcasts.
   In the WFM applet, click the audio mode until it says Digital.
   The cycle is Mono -> Auto Stereo -> Digital. Choose a discovered digital
   program from the Digital program selector when available.
5. Watch the status: Digital acquiring, Digital synced / awaiting audio, and Digital audio
   valid describe different stages. Selecting Digital alone does not mean
   the station has been decoded. Return to Auto Stereo for analog reception.

Limits of this test build
This is an experimental local development build, not an official release.
See BUILD-INFO.json for the actual toolchain, enabled features and executable
signing status. A valid source commit signature does not sign the Windows app.
Windows may warn about an unsigned or unfamiliar application.

Use one RTL receiver and one digital program at a time. Digital reception needs the whole digital
station footprint inside the captured band, and a usable digital signal.
There is no automatic analog fallback. Keep the test receive-only.
Startup and recorded-IQ tests do not establish reception or audible playback
on your radio, PC, antenna, or station. See the separately supplied test report.

Useful feedback
Send the revision above, Windows version, CPU, RTL model, station/frequency,
selected digital program, and whether analog FM works. Note the exact status shown,
time to lock, audio dropouts, channel balance, metadata, and what action caused
any problem. A screenshot of the WFM diagnostics and short reproduction steps
are useful. Review logs before sharing; do not send credentials or raw RF
recordings. Do not send the profile folder as routine feedback.

Source and notices
The matching source is included in source/@SOURCE_ARCHIVE@. Keep it with this
build if you pass the ZIP onward. It contains source, dependency provenance,
patches and build instructions for this checkpoint. licenses/ contains the
AetherSDR and bundled-component notices. Digital decoding is embedded; no external
decoder command-line program or decoder download is needed.

